findings.evidence:
The text reads "Whether AutoResolver diagnoses a real failure correctly (#59) is covered by the scenario feature-stock-refusals". It does not say:
- the proof's own failure text already names each vacuous test;
- the Completion Owner's review named the cause first in all three real 2026-10-04 calls (review_already_named_cause=True 3/3 in the implementer's B6 run);
- a CORRECT shows confirmation plus a bounded repair, not unaided discovery of a product-logic defect;
- no live result exists yet.

scenarios/README.md:171 only says a correct diagnosis "may be a confirmation". Plan D4 puts the full scope statement in the later docs/bugs note, but the testing.md sentence reads as if #59 were already answered.

The claim holds. Nothing forwards the diagnosis guidance to the retried Builder:
- finish_operational_diagnosis (autocode_resolver_runtime.py:916-939) only builds a Proposal payload and records the decision;
- autocode_stage_context.py:195 says "No previous transcripts or history array is forwarded";
- no other module reads payload['guidance'].

The guidance lives in Decision.payload, which is saved beside the receipt in the runner-owned resolver/<key>.json record (autocode_resolver_runtime.py:524-528) and in the ledger cache. The Receipt dataclass (autocode_resolver.py:78-98) has no payload field. "Recorded only with the policy decision" would be exact.
